From cf0a267f78987926c79e3594e418eb3a3e26055b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virt-ios <virt-ios@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:32:52 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] apple-gfx with reims-vgpu on Windows

memory-backend-section (Windows only): guest RAM on a pagefile-backed
section, mapped at a 2 MiB-aligned address (a placeholder replaced by the
view), registered so apple-gfx can hand reims-vgpu the section HANDLE in
RvgMemoryRangeFile.fd (Windows handles are 32-bit significant); the
library maps its views of guest pages from it, as it does from
memory-backend-memfd,share=on on Linux.

meson: reims-vgpu (pvg) is looked up on Windows, and CONFIG_MAC_PVG is set
for aarch64-softmmu under TCG there as on Linux.

Verified: qemu-system-aarch64.exe links libreims_vgpu.a (windows-gnu,
UCRT64), contains apple-gfx-mmio and lists memory-backend-section; no
guest booted yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
